WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.699 --> 00:00:04.950
What’s up guys, my name is Colin McNeil
for theScore esports.

00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:09.730
A game Dota 2 can and often does revolve around
Roshan.

00:00:09.730 --> 00:00:13.440
The items he drops can be the key
between victory and defeat.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:17.580
So it’s no surprise that a lot of the game's most memorable plays

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:20.240
have been in and around the Rosh pit.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:27.020
From Aegis steals, to denies, to ganks, to baits,
here are the Top 10 Roshan Plays.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:35.410
Holding the record for the youngest player
to ever win TI, our number 10 play sees Sumail

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.410
put on a show inside the Roshan pit.

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:45.760
In Game 3 of the 2017 Kiev Major, Sumail blinks
into the pit and lands an insane, five-man coil

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:49.360
to completely wipe SG and secure the Aegis.

00:00:49.840 --> 00:01:24.640
(Casting)

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:31.040
Known for their early Roshan kills, No Tidehunter
comes in at number 9

00:01:31.040 --> 00:01:35.600
with a creative play that lured EG into a deathtrap.

00:01:35.680 --> 00:01:42.390
During Dreamhack Winter 2012’s grand final,
AdmiralBulldog sacrifices his life to Roshan,

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:48.320
replicating a failed kill, as he baits EG
towards him for a gank to remember.

00:01:48.320 --> 00:02:31.680
(Casting)

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:39.160
Dota 2 is a game that isn’t short on creative
plays, and number 8 on our list shows us just that.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:45.440
In the G-1 Champions League Season 5 Finals,
Alliance stuns everyone with an incredible

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:51.200
Level 1 Roshan steal, so early, that even
the casters were caught off guard.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:03:39.680
(Casting)

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.160
Our 
number 7 play sees, S4 come out of nowhere

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:50.080
to absolutely blind-side Ad Finem, as he jumps
in the pit to steal the Aegis

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.800
and turn the tide in OG’s favor.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:04:19.200
(Casting)

00:04:20.480 --> 00:04:25.920
Coming in at number 6 is MMY’s cheeky play
to steal Roshan and deny the Aegis

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:33.920
with only familiars against CDEC.Young during Game 1
of The Summit 4 China Lower-Bracket Qualifiers.

00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:49.440
(Casting)

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.980
Number 5 goes to EG’s Cr1t, who pulls off
an incredible play as he jumps into the pit

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:00.160
against compLexity to steal both Roshan and
the Aegis,

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.720
topping it off with a kill onto Limmp.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:43.680
(Casting)

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:50.720
Number 4 on our list is a god like play that sees Liquid’s GH deny Secret’s Puppey

00:05:50.840 --> 00:05:56.420
and KheZu of the Rosh steal during an elimination game at TI7.

00:05:56.420 --> 00:06:19.240
(Casting)

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:26.480
The third spot on our list goes to the legendary Six Million Dollar Echo Slam at TI5

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:34.040
With CDEC grouped up tight in the pit, PPD and Universe went in with am Ancient Apparition-Earthshaker wombo combo

00:06:34.040 --> 00:06:41.400
that utterly shredded CDEC’s health bars, effectively winning the game then and there.

00:06:41.440 --> 00:07:19.360
(Casting)

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:24.400
There are many kinds of plays in Dota 2, but

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:29.440
the difference between average and amazing lies right here, at number 2.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:35.840
During Game 3 of DreamLeague Season 8 versus
Mineski, Abed single-handedly carries Fnatic

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:38.400
and pulls off a game-saving play

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.680
that sees him secure a three-man kill and steal everything from Mineski.

00:07:43.680 --> 00:08:19.360
(Casting)

00:08:20.080 --> 00:08:23.240
Steamrolling past the competition at number
1 on our list

00:08:23.240 --> 00:08:27.240
is none other than ah fu’s disgusting Aegis steal.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:33.040
During the semi-final match of TI7 between
Virtus Pro and LGD Forever Young,

00:08:33.040 --> 00:08:36.880
ah fu leaps into the Rosh Pit as he snatches away the Aegis

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:40.760
in a play that could only be described as larceny.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:09:22.480
(Casting)

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:24.280
Well guys that’s our list.

00:09:24.280 --> 00:09:27.440
But If you thought we missed out on a sick Roshan play

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:31.520
that should have been in this Top 10, keep it to yourself okay?

